% Wave-4 batch A capstone: the real upstream SATySFi 0.1 `std-ja-book`
% document class (dist-v01/packages/std-ja-book.satyh — a near-clone
% sibling of the already-proven std-ja capstone, plus a footnote
% facility), driving the FULL pipeline: V0_1 lex -> cst_v1 parse -> loader
% (`@require:` transitive resolution across annot/math/code/footnote-
% scheme/hyph-english/unidata/the 4 font stand-ins/the stdlib leaf
% packages) -> v1 lowering -> shared elaborate/typecheck(V0_1)/sealing ->
% eval -> line break -> page break -> PDF. Latin-only, math-free,
% show-toc left at its `false` default and \figure never called (both
% would pull in CJK glyphs — `目次`/`図` literals baked into the class
% itself — that the single-DejaVu-face G7 font stand-in cannot render),
% exactly mirroring `v01-stdja.saty`'s own Latin-only-body discipline.
@require: std-ja-book

StdJaBook.document (|
  title  = {SATySFi in Rust: The Book Capstone},
  author = {The Vendoring Agents},
|) '<
  +StdJaBook.p {
    This is a real upstream SATySFi 0.1 document class, std-ja-book,
    rendered end to end through the Rust port.
  }
  +StdJaBook.section{Introduction}<
    +StdJaBook.p {
      This section proves that the book class's title-page deco and
      section rules compile and render through the real pipeline.
    }
  >
  +StdJaBook.section{Conclusion}<
    +StdJaBook.p {
      The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog.\StdJaBook.footnote{A trailing footnote, proving FootnoteScheme.main renders through page-break.}
    }
  >
>
